    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40309" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quō-vīs</span></b> , adv.
		quivis, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to any place whatever</i> (<b>poet.</b>): cibo perduci poteris quovis. <i><span class="en">Plaut. Most.
				4, 2, 7</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quovis admittunt aves,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					As. 2, 1, 11</span></i>
			.—With <i>gentium</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">immo abeat quovis gentium,</span>”
				<i>let him go anywhere in the world</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Heaut. 5, 1, 55</span></i>
			.</div>
